second begins.\nInformation propagates according to the dependencies and propagation semantics of the network.\nReason about topology\nWhen reading or writing a network:\n* Treat declarations as simultaneously existing relationships.\n* Represent dependencies through connections.\n* Allow propagation to follow available information.\n* Avoid using source-code order to express control flow.\n* Make ordering, buffering, and timing explicit when necessary.\n* Consider feedback, convergence, and conflicting information.\nA network is a persistent organization of relationships whose information state may evolve.\nAnti-pattern: imperative thinking disguised as propagators\nAn agent may translate each step of a procedural algorithm into a separate propagator while retaining the original execution sequence.\nThis can produce syntactically valid Lain code with little benefit from the language’s relational capabilities.\nCorrection: Reconsider the problem as a network of constraints and interactions. Determine which dependencies are intrinsic to the domain and which were introduced by the procedural decomposition.\n\n⸻\n\n\n\n## language-introduction-cell\nLain is a connected dataflow language, not Clojure. Return raw parenthesized forms only; triple-backtick fences are invalid source. A callable is invoked as (f x); (-> x f) writes to the callable cell and does NOT call f. Only binding/argument vectors use literal brackets; construct data vectors with seq:empty and seq:append. Temporal sources accept occurrences from event:point, never bare message records or other behavior objects. A scan takes its source as its first argument; do not write events to the scan result. behavior:scan, map, and event-filter produce behavior objects, not ordinary records or vectors. Use behavior:latest-value to project a selected behavior value before passing to ordinary primitives. An optional fallback makes an empty behavior usable without inventing an occurrence. seq:project projects one key, so (seq:project :role xs) returns role strings, not message records. Model messages must be records with string :role and :content. System instructions must be first. The user ingress is a message RECORD, not a behavior or callable. You must capture its occurrences with event:point if you need a temporal source. (define name expression) binds a cell. (define pending) declares an unknown cell. (network [x y] expression) defines a callable. (let [x expression y expression] body) binds locals. (-> value target-cell) connects cells. (if condition yes no) selects a branch. Qualified names avoid editor collisions. Use data:record for immutable plain records, NOT struct, when passing data to primitives. (data:record :key value) constructs a record; (data:get :key record) reads it. seq:empty [] returns an empty vector; seq:append [vector element] appends one element; seq:concat [vector ...] concatenates vectors into one flat vector; for example (seq:concat (seq:append (seq:empty) 1) (seq:append (seq:empty) 2)) returns a vector containing 1 and 2; seq:last [vector] reads the last element. seq:project [key vector] projects a key over a vector. data:equal? [a b] compares values. event:point [id numeric-time value] captures a retained temporal occurrence. Each identity is immutable: later changes at its input do not withdraw earlier occurrences; connect its output to a behavior:source or scan. text:format [template & values] formats %s placeholders; for example (text:format \"item %s\" 7). Example individual operations: (define values (behavior:source)); (-> (event:point \"sample\" 1 7) values); (define sums (behavior:scan values + 0)). behavior:source [] creates a reducer cell; connect supported event:point results to it with ->. behavior:scan [source reducer initial] emits a state at EVERY ordered occurrence: each state is the corresponding accumulated prefix, not merely the final state. It uses a pure two-argument Lain callable; maps, filters, and reducers construct values and must not perform IO. Callback invocation uses a frozen temporary network, so callbacks must use their explicit arguments and immutable constants; reading changing external cells does not read the live network. behavior:event-filter [behavior predicate] keeps matching historical occurrences and their values. If a new occurrence is rejected, the last previously accepted occurrence remains available: latest-value of the filtered behavior stays unchanged. The predicate receives each behavior VALUE, which may itself be a vector or record. behavior:map [behavior callable] maps values. behavior:latest-value [behavior optional-fallback] projects its most recent value to an ordinary supported cell; before the first occurrence it returns the optional fallback, or remains unknown if no fallback was supplied. For example (behavior:latest-value values 0). Repeated identical events are suppressed; sources and scans are independent. model:request [record] submits { :id string :messages vector-of-role-content-records } to the existing model. Roles are strings system/user/assistant; content is a string. user-ingress publishes a record with :id, :time (odd integer), :role user, :content. Assistant time should be user time + 1 and assistant id must differ from user id. message-to-user [record] acknowledges a record containing :id :time :role assistant :content and returns that record with :acknowledged true. Its output, not generated source, is the delivered message. source:admit [complete-reply lexical-target support-cell-reference] admits complete forms sequentially, preserving earlier forms if a later one fails. environment:overview [environment optional-name-vector] lists visible binding titles, short headlines and references, including unknowns. The optional vector selects which bindings also include their full content; it does not recursively expand values. cell:reference [cell] yields an inspectable reference without waiting for its value. inspect:cell [reference] exposes only :edge, :value (strongest value), :inputs (producing connections), and :outputs (consuming connections). cell:value [reference] connects that edge's strongest value directly to an ordinary cell. cell:input [reference] returns a writable port for the referenced edge. Memory record fields contain references, so write through cell:input, not into a slot read projection. data:snapshot [compound] resolves a finite compound into a plain record; unknown slots remain pending. Use inspect:cell for edge/value/input/output inspection.\n\n## dynamic-expressions-cell\nEvery expression builds connected propagators. A function call whose operands are cells is reactive: it recomputes when their strongest values change. event:point is NOT limited to literal IDs and times. data:get extracts fields reactively. No callback, listener or new source compilation is needed for each input. Never bypass event:point to make inputs dynamic.\nOperators: event:point, data:get\nPurpose: Convert connected identity, time and payload inputs into retained temporal occurrences. Arguments may change reactively.\nLain source:\n(define doc:changing-reading)\n(define doc:changing-source (behavior:source))\n(-> (event:point (data:get :id doc:changing-reading) (data:get :time doc:changing-reading) (data:get :value doc:changing-reading)) doc:changing-source)\n(define doc:changing-prefixes (behavior:scan doc:changing-source seq:append (seq:empty)))\n(define doc:changing-values (behavior:latest-value doc:changing-prefixes (seq:empty)))\nExpected observations (test metadata):\n[{:binding \"doc:changing-values\" :kind :value :expected [7 11]}] :publications [{:binding \"doc:changing-reading\" :value {:id \"reading-1\" :time 1 :value 7} :observed \"doc:changing-values\" :expected [7]} {:binding \"doc:changing-reading\" :value {:id \"reading-2\" :time 2 :value 11} :observed \"doc:changing-values\" :expected [7 11]}]\nVerification publishes reading-1/time=1/value=7, then replaces the same input cell with reading-2/time=2/value=11. Without recompilation the projected vector changes from [7] to [7 11]. These publications are test metadata; this is documentation, not an installed running example.\n\n\n## user-ingress\nState: unknown. unknown\n\n## orientation-result-cell\n{:value 5, :edge {:edge #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"42f6e2d7-cb03-3ba4-8b04-b4120b01293d\"}, :value 5, :inputs #{#propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"01a1ad2e-66c3-7b75-8d8d-9e51cfb4dec2\"} #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"92ebcc51-a460-3f8f-b92e-cf10bc51afd7\"} #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"2ea7aafd-15b4-37a7-bcba-4b2f8f6838f2\"} #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"5cabdd9a-6fc5-39aa-94bf-cafd5e71853d\"} #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"01a1ad2e-6774-7b02-9ea7-73682c75d2f4\"}}, :outputs #{#propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"01a1ad2e-6774-7b02-9ea7-73682c75d2f3\"} #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"a055d368-680e-319e-a2e5-26838514c002\"} #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"01a1ad2e-66c3-7b75-8d8d-9e51cfb4dec1\"} #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"2d0b0130-ed36-344c-8fd6-fe2a83b7d256\"} #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"92ebcc51-a460-3f8f-b92e-cf10bc51afd7\"} #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"01a1ad2e-66c3-7b75-8d8d-9e51cfb4dec3\"} #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"01a1ad2e-6774-7b02-9ea7-73682c75d2f5\"} #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"5cabdd9a-6fc5-39aa-94bf-cafd5e71853d\"}}}}\n\n## history\n[{:sequence 1, :request-id \"setup\", :source \"\\n\\n(define orient:source (behavior:source))\\n(-> (event:point \\\"orient-a\\\" 1 2) orient:source)\\n(-> (event:point \\\"orient-b\\\" 2 3) orient:source)\\n(define orient:sum (behavior:scan orient:source + 0))\\n(define orient:reading (behavior:latest-value orient:sum 0))\\n(-> (cell:value (cell:reference orient:reading)) (cell:input (data:get :orientation-value memory-cell)))\\n(-> (inspect:cell (cell:reference orient:reading)) (cell:input (data:get :orientation-edge memory-cell)))\", :kind :reply}]\n\n## reducer-verification-cell\nVerified through compiled Lain, not a simulated conversation: a numeric source with occurrences 1@1 and 2@2, scanned with seq:append and an empty vector seed, emits prefix values [1] and [1,2]. Filtering those prefix values by whether their last number is greater than 1 keeps [1,2]. A later 0@3 is rejected by that predicate, leaving the filtered latest value [1,2]. The unfiltered scan advances to [1,2,0]. Exact replay produces no new values, and another source remains independent. Each call to behavior:source creates a new independent instance. A scan compiled into the lexical admission target also reduced an occurrence 5@1 with + and seed 0 to 5.\n\n## construction-review-cell\nA previous generated setup compiled but did not connect requests or history. Diagnostic review: each call to behavior:source creates a DISTINCT source, so writing to another unnamed instance does not feed a previously created scan. Event identity and time must vary with actual events; constants user/1 and assistant/2 cannot identify three turns. A bare acknowledged record must be converted to a temporal occurrence before feeding a temporal source. A callable inside behavior:map or scan is evaluated as a pure transformation; model:request and message-to-user must run in the live network, never inside a temporal transformation callback. seq:project with key :role returns strings and therefore is unsuitable as the request messages vector. No generated definitions from previous attempts exist in this fresh child.\n\n## operator-examples-cell\nConcrete executable examples and expected results for the advertised operators. Each example is independent and uses doc:* names. Core libraries and experiment capabilities are already installed. Tests compile these exact sources; no example implements a conversation history network. Effects are tested with controlled transport and the real session delivery extension. Read expected observations as test metadata, not additional Lain forms.\n\nOperators: define, network, let, if\nPurpose: Bind cells and define a callable network; invoke the callable with connected arguments.\nLain source:\n(define doc:increment (network [x] (let [next (+ x 1)] (if (> next 0) next 0))))\n(define doc:incremented (doc:increment 4))\nExpected observations (test metadata):\n[{:binding \"doc:incremented\" :kind :value :expected 5}]\n\nOperators: ->, def-cells\nPurpose: Connect a source value to a target cell. This propagates values; it does not call a function.\nLain source:\n(def-cells doc:raw doc:forwarded)\n(-> 7 doc:raw)\n(-> doc:raw doc:forwarded)\nExpected observations (test metadata):\n[{:binding \"doc:forwarded\" :kind :value :expected 7}]\n\nOperators: |>, compose\nPurpose: Pipe a value through callables; compose creates a reusable composition.\nLain source:\n(define doc:plus-one (network [x] (+ x 1)))\n(define doc:twice (network [x] (* x 2)))\n(define doc:piped (|> 3 doc:plus-one doc:twice))\n(define doc:composed ((compose doc:plus-one doc:twice) 3))\nExpected observations (test metadata):\n[{:binding \"doc:piped\" :kind :value :expected 8} {:binding \"doc:composed\" :kind :value :expected 7}]\n\nOperators: struct, slot\nPurpose: Construct a compound with named slots and connect through its slot projections.\nLain source:\n(define doc:port)\n(define doc:object (struct :nested (struct :value doc:port)))\n(-> 42 (|> doc:object (slot :nested) (slot :value)))\nExpected observations (test metadata):\n[{:binding \"doc:port\" :kind :value :expected 42}]\n\nOperators: <->\nPurpose: Connect two cells bidirectionally so either can supply information.\nLain source:\n(def-cells doc:left doc:right)\n(<-> doc:left doc:right)\n(-> 9 doc:right)\nExpected observations (test metadata):\n[{:binding \"doc:left\" :kind :value :expected 9}]\n\nOperators: let-cell, constraint:+\nPurpose: Declare local cells and relate them with arithmetic constraints.\nLain source:\n(define doc:average (network [a b] (let-cell [total] (constraint:+ a b total) (/ total 2))))\n(define doc:average-value (doc:average 3 7))\nExpected observations (test metadata):\n[{:binding \"doc:average-value\" :kind :value :expected 5}]\n\nOperators: cond\nPurpose: Choose a result from condition/value pairs, with an else fallback.\nLain source:\n(define doc:classification (cond [(< 0 0) :negative (= 0 0) :zero else :positive]))\nExpected observations (test metadata):\n[{:binding \"doc:classification\" :kind :value :expected :zero}]\n\nOperators: list, car, cdr\nPurpose: Construct a linked list and access its first element or remaining tail.\nLain source:\n(define doc:list-first (car (list 4 5)))\n(define doc:list-second (car (cdr (list 4 5))))\nExpected observations (test metadata):\n[{:binding \"doc:list-first\" :kind :value :expected 4} {:binding \"doc:list-second\" :kind :value :expected 5}]\n\nOperators: +, -, *, /, >, <, =\nPurpose: Compute arithmetic values and comparisons from connected operands.\nLain source:\n(define doc:arithmetic (+ (* 2 3) (- 8 5) (/ 4 2)))\n(define doc:comparison (if (> 3 2) (< 1 2) (= 0 1)))\nExpected observations (test metadata):\n[{:binding \"doc:arithmetic\" :kind :value :expected 11} {:binding \"doc:comparison\" :kind :value :expected true}]\n\nOperators: data:record\nPurpose: Construct a plain immutable record from key/value pairs.\nLain source:\n(define doc:record (data:record :score 7 :label \"north\"))\nExpected observations (test metadata):\n[{:binding \"doc:record\" :kind :value :expected {:score 7 :label \"north\"}}]\n\nOperators: data:get\nPurpose: Read a field from a record; the result updates when the record changes.\nLain source:\n(define doc:field (data:get :score (data:record :score 7)))\nExpected observations (test metadata):\n[{:binding \"doc:field\" :kind :value :expected 7}]\n\nOperators: data:equal?\nPurpose: Compare two ordinary values for equality.\nLain source:\n(define doc:equal (data:equal? (data:record :score 7) (data:record :score 7)))\nExpected observations (test metadata):\n[{:binding \"doc:equal\" :kind :value :expected true}]\n\nOperators: data:merge\nPurpose: Merge plain records into a new record.\nLain source:\n(define doc:merged (data:merge (data:record :a 1) (data:record :b 2)))\nExpected observations (test metadata):\n[{:binding \"doc:merged\" :kind :value :expected {:a 1 :b 2}}]\n\nOperators: data:snapshot\nPurpose: Resolve the slots of a finite compound into an ordinary record.\nLain source:\n(define doc:snapshot (data:snapshot (struct :score 7)))\nExpected observations (test metadata):\n[{:binding \"doc:snapshot\" :kind :value :expected {:score 7}}]\n\nOperators: seq:empty\nPurpose: Create an empty vector to seed ordinary sequence operations.\nLain source:\n(define doc:empty (seq:empty))\nExpected observations (test metadata):\n[{:binding \"doc:empty\" :kind :value :expected []}]\n\nOperators: seq:append\nPurpose: Append one element to a vector; appending a vector creates a nested vector.\nLain source:\n(define doc:appended (seq:append (seq:empty) 7))\nExpected observations (test metadata):\n[{:binding \"doc:appended\" :kind :value :expected [7]}]\n\nOperators: seq:concat\nPurpose: Concatenate vectors into one flat vector.\nLain source:\n(define doc:concatenated (seq:concat (seq:append (seq:empty) 1) (seq:append (seq:empty) 2)))\nExpected observations (test metadata):\n[{:binding \"doc:concatenated\" :kind :value :expected [1 2]}]\n\nOperators: seq:last\nPurpose: Read the final element of an ordinary vector, not a behavior.\nLain source:\n(define doc:last (seq:last (seq:append (seq:append (seq:empty) 5) 9)))\nExpected observations (test metadata):\n[{:binding \"doc:last\" :kind :value :expected 9}]\n\nOperators: seq:project\nPurpose: Extract one field from each record in a vector.\nLain source:\n(define doc:labels (seq:project :label (seq:append (seq:append (seq:empty) (data:record :label \"north\")) (data:record :label \"south\"))))\nExpected observations (test metadata):\n[{:binding \"doc:labels\" :kind :value :expected [\"north\" \"south\"]}]\n\nOperators: seq:count\nPurpose: Count elements in an ordinary vector.\nLain source:\n(define doc:count (seq:count (seq:append (seq:empty) 7)))\nExpected observations (test metadata):\n[{:binding \"doc:count\" :kind :value :expected 1}]\n\nOperators: text:format\nPurpose: Format text using a template and connected values.\nLain source:\n(define doc:formatted (text:format \"item %s\" 7))\nExpected observations (test metadata):\n[{:binding \"doc:formatted\" :kind :value :expected \"item 7\"}]\n\nOperators: event:point\nPurpose: Convert connected identity, time and payload inputs into retained temporal occurrences. Arguments may change reactively.\nLain source:\n(define doc:event (event:point \"sample-event\" 1 7))\nExpected observations (test metadata):\n[{:binding \"doc:event\" :kind :value :expected {:temporal/type :point :id \"sample-event\" :time 1 :revision 0 :value 7}}]\n\nOperators: behavior:source\nPurpose: Create one independent temporal source that receives explicit occurrences.\nLain source:\n(define doc:source (behavior:source))\n(-> (event:point \"source-event\" 1 7) doc:source)\n(define doc:source-value (behavior:latest-value doc:source))\nExpected observations (test metadata):\n[{:binding \"doc:source-value\" :kind :value :expected 7}]\n\nOperators: behavior:scan\nPurpose: Reduce ordered occurrences into accumulated prefixes, using a pure two-argument function and initial value.\nLain source:\n(define doc:scan-input (behavior:source))\n(-> (event:point \"scan-a\" 1 1) doc:scan-input)\n(-> (event:point \"scan-b\" 2 2) doc:scan-input)\n(define doc:scan (behavior:scan doc:scan-input + 0))\nExpected observations (test metadata):\n[{:binding \"doc:scan\" :kind :behavior-values :expected [1 3]}]\n\nOperators: behavior:map\nPurpose: Transform each temporal value with a pure function; the result remains a behavior.\nLain source:\n(define doc:map-input (behavior:source))\n(-> (event:point \"map-event\" 1 7) doc:map-input)\n(define doc:mapped (behavior:map doc:map-input (network [x] (* x 2))))\nExpected observations (test metadata):\n[{:binding \"doc:mapped\" :kind :behavior-values :expected [14]}]\n\nOperators: behavior:event-filter\nPurpose: Keep temporal occurrences whose values satisfy a pure predicate.\nLain source:\n(define doc:filter-input (behavior:source))\n(-> (event:point \"filter-a\" 1 1) doc:filter-input)\n(-> (event:point \"filter-b\" 2 2) doc:filter-input)\n(-> (event:point \"filter-c\" 3 0) doc:filter-input)\n(define doc:filtered (behavior:event-filter doc:filter-input (network [x] (> x 1))))\n(define doc:filtered-latest (behavior:latest-value doc:filtered))\nExpected observations (test metadata):\n[{:binding \"doc:filtered\" :kind :behavior-values :expected [2]} {:binding \"doc:filtered-latest\" :kind :value :expected 2}]\n\nOperators: behavior:latest-value\nPurpose: Project the latest behavior value into an ordinary cell, with an optional fallback for an empty behavior.\nLain source:\n(define doc:empty-behavior (behavior:source))\n(define doc:fallback (behavior:latest-value doc:empty-behavior 42))\n(define doc:latest-input (behavior:source))\n(-> (event:point \"latest-event\" 1 7) doc:latest-input)\n(define doc:latest (behavior:latest-value doc:latest-input))\nExpected observations (test metadata):\n[{:binding \"doc:fallback\" :kind :value :expected 42} {:binding \"doc:latest\" :kind :value :expected 7}]\n\nOperators: cell:reference\nPurpose: Obtain a cell reference without waiting for its value.\nLain source:\n(define doc:referenced 7)\n(define doc:reference (cell:reference doc:referenced))\nExpected observations (test metadata):\n[{:binding \"doc:reference\" :kind :reference-of :target \"doc:referenced\"}]\n\nOperators: inspect:cell\nPurpose: Inspect an edge's value and its producing and consuming connections.\nLain source:\n(define doc:inspected-value 7)\n(define doc:inspection (inspect:cell (cell:reference doc:inspected-value)))\nExpected observations (test metadata):\n[{:binding \"doc:inspection\" :kind :cell-view :expected 7}]\n\nOperators: empty-env\nPurpose: Create an empty lexical environment.\nLain source:\n(define doc:empty-environment (empty-env))\nExpected observations (test metadata):\n[{:binding \"doc:empty-environment\" :kind :environment}]\n\nOperators: lexical-child\nPurpose: Create an independent lexical child that inherits parent bindings.\nLain source:\n(define doc:parent (empty-env))\n(define doc:child (lexical-child doc:parent))\nExpected observations (test metadata):\n[{:binding \"doc:child\" :kind :child-of :parent \"doc:parent\"}]\n\nOperators: env:slot\nPurpose: Create a binding contribution for an argument cell.\nLain source:\n(define doc:binding-value 7)\n(define doc:contribution (env:slot \"score\" doc:binding-value))\nExpected observations (test metadata):\n[{:binding \"doc:contribution\" :kind :contribution :name \"score\" :expected 7}]\n\nOperators: extend-env, environment:overview\nPurpose: Extend a lexical environment with a contribution; overview returns structured binding descriptions.\nLain source:\n(define doc:extended (extend-env (empty-env) (env:slot \"doc-score\" 7)))\n(define doc:overview (environment:overview doc:extended))\nExpected observations (test metadata):\n[{:binding \"doc:overview\" :kind :overview-has :title \"doc-score\" :headline \"7\"}]\n\nOperators: model:request\nPurpose: Invoke the existing model with text or a flat vector of role/content records. Defining a wrapper does not invoke it.\nLain source:\n(define doc:model-receipt (model:request (data:record :id \"doc-model-probe\" :messages (seq:append (seq:empty) (data:record :role \"user\" :content \"Return only (define doc-model-generated 42)\")))))\nExpected observations (test metadata):\n[{:binding \"doc:model-receipt\" :kind :value :expected :completed} {:binding \"model-result\" :kind :model-response :request \"doc-model-probe\"}]\n\nOperators: message-to-user\nPurpose: Deliver a message record and obtain its delivery acknowledgement.\nLain source:\n(define doc:delivery (message-to-user (data:record :id \"doc-delivery\" :time 1 :role \"assistant\" :content \"operator probe\")))\nExpected observations (test metadata):\n[{:binding \"doc:delivery\" :kind :acknowledgement :content \"operator probe\"}]\n\nOperators: source:admit\nPurpose: Admit a completed source response into a lexical target, retaining receipts and successful prefix forms.\nLain source:\n(define doc:admission-target (lexical-child (empty-env)))\n(define doc:complete-response (data:record :request-id \"doc-admission\" :kind :reply :text \"(define doc-admitted-value 42)\" :thinking \"\" :finish-reason \"stop\" :truncated? false))\n(define doc:admission (source:admit doc:complete-response doc:admission-target (cell:reference doc:complete-response)))\nExpected observations (test metadata):\n[{:binding \"doc:admission\" :kind :admission :target \"doc:admission-target\" :name \"doc-admitted-value\" :expected 42}]\n\nOperators: cell:value\nPurpose: Observe the strongest value at a referenced cell.\nLain source:\n(define doc:strongest-input 7)\n(define doc:strongest (cell:value (cell:reference doc:strongest-input)))\nExpected observations (test metadata):\n[{:binding \"doc:strongest\" :kind :value :expected 7}]\n\nOperators: memory-cell\nPurpose: Write a strongest value through a parent memory port, read it back, and use it in a model request.\nLain source:\n(define doc:memory-source 7)\n(-> (cell:value (cell:reference doc:memory-source)) (cell:input (data:get :feedback-value memory-cell)))\n(define doc:remembered (cell:value (data:get :feedback-value memory-cell)))\n(define doc:memory-feedback (model:request (data:record :id \"doc-memory-probe\" :text (text:format \"memory-score=%s\" doc:remembered))))\nExpected observations (test metadata):\n[{:binding \"doc:remembered\" :kind :value :expected 7} {:binding \"doc:memory-feedback\" :kind :value :expected :completed}]\n\nOperators: construct-concept-of\nPurpose: Contribute a named ce